* LDO sizes: the bias branch copies the bandgap branch (m_bias), an NMOS mirror scales it for the amplifier tail (m_amp); the 100 uA bleed is an rppd resistor from the output (w_rb, l_rb), so it holds nearly constant with temperature where a PTAT copy would grow a third by 125 C; the pass follower carries 2 mA rated, 20 mA at most, at about 2.45 V on its gate; the output capacitor is 100 pF of MIM, the gate capacitor (w_cg) sets the light-load phase margin, and l_rf/w_cfl and l_rn/w_cn size the reference and bias filters.
.param m_bias=1 m_amp=4 w_rb=1u l_rb=46u w_nb=4u l_nb=4u w_ein=20u l_ein=2u w_eld=8u l_eld=4u w_pass=600u l_pass=0.45u ng_pass=60 w_cl=258u w_cg=44u l_rn=184u w_cn=52u l_rf=368u w_cfl=82u
